From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase, kernel32, setupapi: find flags, remote protocol info, heap snapshots, config-specific device keys

FIXMEs and stubs, as documented now:

- FindFirstFileExW: FIND_FIRST_EX_CASE_SENSITIVE gives only the names
  that match the mask's case ('*', '?' and the DOS wildcards '<', '>',
  '"'); FIND_FIRST_EX_ON_DISK_ENTRIES_ONLY leaves out entries whose data
  is not on disk (FILE_ATTRIBUTE_RECALL_ON_OPEN, RECALL_ON_DATA_ACCESS);
  any other flag than these and FIND_FIRST_EX_LARGE_FETCH is
  ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER (it was a FIXME and went on).
- GetFileInformationByHandleEx(FileRemoteProtocolInfo) (was
  ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED): for a file on a remote device, its protocol
  (SMB 3, or NFS 4 by the file system's name); for a local file
  ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER; ERROR_BAD_LENGTH for a short buffer.
- CreateToolhelp32Snapshot(TH32CS_SNAPHEAPLIST) (was ERROR_CALL_NOT_
  IMPLEMENTED alone, a FIXME with others): this process's heaps
  (HF32_DEFAULT for the default one); Heap32ListFirst (was a stub),
  Heap32ListNext, Heap32First and Heap32Next (were "@ stub") list them and
  walk their blocks (LF32_FIXED, LF32_MOVEABLE, LF32_FREE). Another
  process's heaps are not walked: its list is empty.
- SetupDiCreateDevRegKey, SetupDiOpenDevRegKey and SetupDiDeleteDevRegKey
  with DICS_FLAG_CONFIGSPECIFIC (a FIXME, then the global key) use the
  hardware profile's branch, System\CurrentControlSet\Hardware Profiles\
  {Current, or the profile number}\System\CurrentControlSet\Enum\<device>
  (DIREG_DEV) or ...\Control\Class\<driver> (DIREG_DRV); under the current
  profile, which wineboot makes volatile, they are volatile too.

Gate: test/fileflags-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/fileflags-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_CASE_INSENSITIVE, SG_MUTANT_REMOTE_FOR_ALL
(kernelbase/file.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_HEAP_WALK (kernel32/toolhelp.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_CONFIG_SPECIFIC (setupapi/devinst.c).
